// TEST: If Numeric Branches Promote
// WARN: BL3020
// ============================================================================
// Numeric branches of different width promote the way `+`'s operands do:
// symmetric, to the join, with the narrower branch widened by an EXPLICIT
// cast node so both lanes agree. A literal adapts silently; a converted
// NON-literal (`n` below) earns the same BL3020 mixed-type arithmetic
// warns with. The old behavior depended on branch order: one order passed
// by accident and the other was accepted by the checker and then refused
// by g++ as a narrowing conversion.
let a = if false then 2.5 else 10
let b = if true then 10 else 2.5
let n = 3
let c = if true then n else 2.5
// EXPECT: a = 10
// EXPECT: b = 10
// EXPECT: c = 3
